mergeNoListT -- mergeStyles does not walk a field with no list (GO 6, 2026-11-27; fixit mergeStylesNoList retired into it).

What it asks. mergeStyles walks a form and merges each field's held style into it. A field with no attribute and
no member has no list, and a for over such a field prints "nextGroup: ERROR <tag> does not contain a list". firstLight's
bar holds one (space), so every show(firstLight) printed that line twice: once from mergeStyles' own loop and once
from resolveLook's, which it calls. Now mergeStyles leaves at once when its field has no list.

The rows.
    mnWith      a field with a list and a held style: the style's strokeColor is merged (red).
    mnBare      its first member, no list: read as it was, length 0, no strokeColor, and nothing on stderr.
    mnKid       the member AFTER the bare one, with its own held style: red. The walk went on past the bare member.
    mnAlone     mergeStyles called on a field with no list directly: nothing, and nothing on stderr.
    stderr      holds no nextGroup line (the harness reads it; this file prints on stdout so stderr can be read whole).
The H7. With noListNoWalk taken out of mergeStyles, stderr holds four nextGroup lines (two a bare field).
